-Nothing for Minneapolis.
-MAN: Anything for Omaha?

1255
00:44:57,997 --> 00:44:59,465
All flights for Omaha
are sold out, sir.

1256
00:44:59,498 --> 00:45:01,300
-Well, how about tomorrow?
-Tomorrow? No.

1257
00:45:01,333 --> 00:45:03,435
-Next week.
-SERVO: Lois Lane got a fro.

1258
00:45:03,468 --> 00:45:04,537
I hope you can help me.

1259
00:45:04,570 --> 00:45:06,505
My wife is very ill in Dallas.

1260
00:45:06,538 --> 00:45:08,807
I can get you a reservation
a week from next Tuesday,

1261
00:45:08,840 --> 00:45:10,075
but you have to get a priority.

1262
00:45:10,108 --> 00:45:12,377
Here's where you apply
for it, sir.

1263
00:45:12,410 --> 00:45:14,112
CROW:
Oh, Noel Neill, Lois number two.

1264
00:45:14,145 --> 00:45:15,580
WOMAN: ...for Gardiner Field,
Montana.

1265
00:45:15,613 --> 00:45:16,915
-Gardiner Field, Montana?
-SERVO: "Can you give me

1266
00:45:16,948 --> 00:45:18,050
a ticket-- Gardiner Field?"

1267
00:45:18,083 --> 00:45:19,818
-Get out of here.
-Is this a business trip?

1268
00:45:19,852 --> 00:45:21,420
No, I wanna go home.

1269
00:45:21,453 --> 00:45:22,653
My husband's there,
and my children.

1270
00:45:22,687 --> 00:45:23,888
They're with him.

1271
00:45:23,922 --> 00:45:25,423
SERVO: I'll save you the time,
they're all dead.

1272
00:45:25,457 --> 00:45:29,027
...all flights to Gardiner Field
have been discontinued.

1273
00:45:29,060 --> 00:45:31,062
-Discontinued?
-SERVO: Mm-hmm.

1274
00:45:31,097 --> 00:45:32,330
For how long?

1275
00:45:32,363 --> 00:45:36,033
-I'm afraid permanently.
-CROW: Ten thousand years.

1276
00:45:36,067 --> 00:45:37,770
There hadn't been an attack.

1277
00:45:37,803 --> 00:45:39,705
Early this morning.

1278
00:45:39,738 --> 00:45:41,940
SERVO: What a stressful airline.

1279
00:45:41,973 --> 00:45:43,342
An A-bomb.

1280
00:45:43,375 --> 00:45:48,147
MIKE: Hey, look, they're dead.
Let's move it along, lady.

1281
00:45:48,180 --> 00:45:50,748
CROW:
The hat squad consoles her.

1282
00:45:50,782 --> 00:45:53,118
SERVO: So, what are you doing
later on, little lady?

1283
00:45:53,152 --> 00:45:55,887
Are you busy or...?

1284
00:45:55,920 --> 00:45:57,790
I don't think we'll do
any good here.

1285
00:45:57,823 --> 00:45:59,692
You know,
there's a bellhop in my hotel,

1286
00:45:59,725 --> 00:46:01,127
you know, with all the angles.

1287
00:46:01,160 --> 00:46:03,628
SERVO: Calls himself Euclid.

1288
00:46:03,662 --> 00:46:06,265
-You're right.
-CROW: Ma'am, we need hookers.

1289
00:46:06,298 --> 00:46:08,000
Anything to get to Phoenix
or Tucson?

1290
00:46:08,033 --> 00:46:09,033
All sold out.

1291
00:46:09,067 --> 00:46:10,335
How about San Francisco?

1292
00:46:10,368 --> 00:46:13,072
Still a few spaces left,
if you can get a priority.

1293
00:46:13,105 --> 00:46:14,573
SERVO: Anything left
for Uriah Heep?

1294
00:46:14,607 --> 00:46:15,840
-...here.
-Thanks.

1295
00:46:15,873 --> 00:46:18,510
You know, I think I'll try
for San Francisco with you.

1296
00:46:18,543 --> 00:46:21,012
Maybe I can rent a car there
and drive home.

1297
00:46:21,045 --> 00:46:23,782
Fine, come along.

1298
00:46:23,815 --> 00:46:25,117
I'd like a ticket to Seattle.

1299
00:46:25,150 --> 00:46:28,087
SERVO: Look, they're dead.

1300
00:46:28,120 --> 00:46:30,088
And when you pledge
to the Soviet Union,

1301
00:46:30,122 --> 00:46:32,157
you get this nifty
tote bag and...

1302
00:46:32,190 --> 00:46:34,793
Are you sure you understood
my instructions?

1303
00:46:34,827 --> 00:46:37,930
SERVO: Idaho, damn it,
show me Idaho.

1304
00:46:37,963 --> 00:46:40,032
We have lost aircraft 8 and 9,

1305
00:46:40,065 --> 00:46:41,833
and there are still two
fields remaining.

1306
00:46:41,867 --> 00:46:43,802
-SERVO: Filter fields.
-Here and here.

1307
00:46:43,835 --> 00:46:46,905
CROW:
Now, show me West Virginia.

1308
00:46:46,938 --> 00:46:48,940
Regardless of loss,
let's concentrate

1309
00:46:48,973 --> 00:46:50,275
two aircrafts on each one.

1310
00:46:50,308 --> 00:46:51,910
[ Indistinct ]
with our own bomb.

1311
00:46:51,943 --> 00:46:53,278
MIKE: [ Indistinct ]
bury the bombs?

1312
00:46:53,312 --> 00:46:55,747
And then order the attack
on San Francisco

1313
00:46:55,780 --> 00:46:56,948
praising the ready stage.

1314
00:46:56,982 --> 00:46:57,983
Immediately, Excellency.

1315
00:46:58,017 --> 00:46:59,283
MIKE: Now,
will the dancing Hitlers,

1316
00:46:59,317 --> 00:47:00,985
please get to this side.

1317
00:47:01,018 --> 00:47:02,787
SERVO: We got a real pretty view
of the dust cloud

1318
00:47:02,820 --> 00:47:03,988
out the right window.

1319
00:47:04,022 --> 00:47:05,990
It's currently 7,000 degrees
in San Francisco.

1320
00:47:06,023 --> 00:47:07,860
MAN: New York, Flight 289,

1321
00:47:07,893 --> 00:47:09,293
to San Francisco tower,

1322
00:47:09,327 --> 00:47:12,130
request landing instructions.

1323
00:47:12,163 --> 00:47:13,265
SERVO: Well, just keep
coming down

1324
00:47:13,298 --> 00:47:14,900
until you're not
in the sky anymore.

1325
00:47:14,933 --> 00:47:16,502
Don't you know how to land?

1326
00:47:16,535 --> 00:47:19,905
-Over.
-Tower to TWA Flight 289,

1327
00:47:19,938 --> 00:47:27,045
land on strip three.

1328
00:47:27,078 --> 00:47:30,415
CROW: Hey, look,
there's Tony Bennett's heart.

1329
00:47:30,448 --> 00:47:32,050
SERVO: They're
on Armageddon location

1330
00:47:32,083 --> 00:47:34,787
in beautiful San Francisco.

1331
00:47:34,820 --> 00:47:37,055
MIKE: If we're real quiet,
maybe, he won't look up.

1332
00:47:37,088 --> 00:47:39,023
SERVO: Shh.

1333
00:47:39,057 --> 00:47:40,425
CROW: Oh, let's go straight
to the wharf.

1334
00:47:40,458 --> 00:47:41,660
MIKE: Oh, Ghirardelli Square.

1335
00:47:41,693 --> 00:47:44,563
SERVO: Oh, PIER 39, please.

1336
00:47:44,597 --> 00:47:46,732
CROW: I really am a cowboy.
We're not gay.

1337
00:47:46,765 --> 00:47:47,732
MAN: This is KRO San Francisco.

1338
00:47:47,765 --> 00:47:50,268
While no A bombs
have fallen on California,

1339
00:47:50,302 --> 00:47:52,237
an unofficial report
from Northern California

1340
00:47:52,270 --> 00:47:54,105
states that six ships
flying the flags

1341
00:47:54,138 --> 00:47:55,440
of six different nations

1342
00:47:55,473 --> 00:47:57,342
were intercepted
by the United States Navy

1343
00:47:57,375 --> 00:48:00,378
and found to be carrying enemy
personnel and equipment.

1344
00:48:00,412 --> 00:48:02,513
Turn it off, will you, mac?

1345
00:48:02,547 --> 00:48:03,682
Anything you say.

1346
00:48:03,715 --> 00:48:08,620
SERVO: Let's just talk.

1347
00:48:08,653 --> 00:48:11,323
The Golden Gate,
there is San Francisco.

1348
00:48:11,357 --> 00:48:13,592
SERVO: Ja,
it's home of Rice-A-Roni.

1349
00:48:13,625 --> 00:48:16,227
MIKE: Ja.

1350
00:48:16,262 --> 00:48:18,363
CROW: Well, it looks like
San Francisco is about to be

1351
00:48:18,397 --> 00:48:20,632
sautéed and simmered.

1352
00:48:20,665 --> 00:48:22,567
SERVO: Hey, you know what?
They're probably going to bomb

1353
00:48:22,600 --> 00:48:25,103
-the Grateful Dead.
-MIKE: Yeah, go, go, go.

1354
00:48:25,137 --> 00:48:27,605
-CROW: And Starship, whoo.
-SERVO: Yeah, whoo.

1355
00:48:27,638 --> 00:48:28,873
Open fire.

1356
00:48:28,907 --> 00:48:30,342
[ Cannon fire ]

1357
00:48:30,375 --> 00:48:35,713
CROW: Go away, you
poopy-caca-head Russians.

1358
00:48:35,747 --> 00:48:37,615
[ Cannon fire continues ]

1359
00:48:37,648 --> 00:48:40,018
SERVO: I mean, I'm from Texas,
that's why I dress this way.

1360
00:48:40,052 --> 00:48:41,553
-I'm not gay.
-What's that?

1361
00:48:41,587 --> 00:48:46,090
MIKE: It's the end of the world
as we know it, and I feel fine.

1362
00:48:46,123 --> 00:48:47,225
It's a B-29.

1363
00:48:47,258 --> 00:48:49,127
CROW: Why is Knute Rockne,
All-American,

1364
00:48:49,160 --> 00:48:51,228
piloting the plane?

1365
00:48:51,262 --> 00:48:52,463
There is the target.

1366
00:48:52,497 --> 00:48:54,565
SERVO: Good, I got to pick up
some light bulbs.

1367
00:48:54,598 --> 00:48:55,767
I love that one.

1368
00:48:55,800 --> 00:48:57,035
CROW: Mantis.

1369
00:48:57,068 --> 00:48:59,037
MAN: Bombs away.

1370
00:48:59,070 --> 00:49:01,238
CROW: Help the bombardier.

1371
00:49:01,272 --> 00:49:02,707
SERVO: You know,
they'll bomb Bobby McFerrin,

1372
00:49:02,740 --> 00:49:03,742
and Robin Williams.

1373
00:49:03,775 --> 00:49:05,643
-Hurray!
-MIKE: Yes.

1374
00:49:05,677 --> 00:49:08,513
[ Cannon fire ]

1375
00:49:08,547 --> 00:49:10,215
Servo: B-29.

1376
00:49:10,248 --> 00:49:12,417
MIKE: Well, we got them,
might as well use them.

1377
00:49:12,450 --> 00:49:19,090
[ Bombs whistling,
explosions ]

1378
00:49:19,123 --> 00:49:25,597
-CROW: Hey, you see all kinds.
-Up ahead, pull up to the curb.

1379
00:49:25,597 --> 00:49:28,933
CROW: I can't stop.
I can't stop.

1380
00:49:29,000 --> 00:49:31,603
[ Cannon fire ]

1381
00:49:31,637 --> 00:49:36,608
SERVO: They're just shooting
caps off on a post card.

1382
00:49:36,608 --> 00:49:40,345
Squibs.

1383
00:49:40,378 --> 00:49:42,180
CROW: Well, shall we go
in the conference room,

1384
00:49:42,213 --> 00:49:44,615
where it's quieter?

1385
00:49:44,648 --> 00:49:45,317
This is awful.

1386
00:49:45,350 --> 00:49:46,418
How do you like
them guys?

1387
00:49:46,452 --> 00:49:47,485
...San Francisco yet.

1388
00:49:47,518 --> 00:49:49,320
They never got bombed
in the last war.

1389
00:49:49,353 --> 00:49:50,655
You never got it, brother.

1390
00:49:50,688 --> 00:49:52,457
-I was in Guadal...
-MIKE: Oh, excuse me.

1391
00:49:52,490 --> 00:49:54,625
Mind if I get a cigarette?

1392
00:49:54,658 --> 00:49:55,327
Have a cigar.

1393
00:49:55,360 --> 00:49:56,395
Oh, thanks.

1394
00:49:56,428 --> 00:49:58,163
-MIKE: Better.
-Anybody got a light?

1395
00:49:58,197 --> 00:49:59,865
CROW: I think I hear one coming.

1396
00:49:59,898 --> 00:50:04,102
[ Explosion ]

1397
00:50:04,135 --> 00:50:07,538
What's the chance of hiring your
cab to drive me there and go...?

1398
00:50:07,572 --> 00:50:10,742
SERVO: Come on,
would you light my cigar?

1399
00:50:10,775 --> 00:50:12,743
Good luck.

1400
00:50:12,777 --> 00:50:15,780
SERVO: Stop it!

1401
00:50:15,813 --> 00:50:17,848
You know, it's funny the world
is coming to an end,

1402
00:50:17,882 --> 00:50:19,818
but you and I are sitting here
having dinner?

1403
00:50:19,852 --> 00:50:20,852
SERVO: Funny ha-ha or?

1404
00:50:20,885 --> 00:50:22,053
Boy, I was hungry.

1405
00:50:22,087 --> 00:50:23,222
I know what you mean.

1406
00:50:23,255 --> 00:50:24,757
CROW: Yeah,
you ate all my food, you pig.

1407
00:50:24,790 --> 00:50:27,158
Every once in a while, I forget
what's happening in the world.

1408
00:50:27,192 --> 00:50:28,627
-SERVO: I'm just dumb.
-And feel good.

1409
00:50:28,660 --> 00:50:29,895
MIKE: I have valium blackouts.

1410
00:50:29,928 --> 00:50:32,263
As if I just met a new beau.

1411
00:50:32,297 --> 00:50:34,933
-You have.
-SERVO: Enjoy my headshot.

1412
00:50:34,967 --> 00:50:38,002
One I like very much.

1413
00:50:38,035 --> 00:50:39,237
He likes you even more.

1414
00:50:39,270 --> 00:50:43,342
CROW: Taster's Choice,
the final chapter.

1415
00:50:43,375 --> 00:50:45,277
-SERVO: Yeah.
-War or no war,

1416
00:50:45,310 --> 00:50:46,412
people have to eat and drink.

1417
00:50:46,445 --> 00:50:48,713
MIKE: Still got to use
the crapper.

1418
00:50:48,747 --> 00:50:50,615
Or make love.

1419
00:50:50,648 --> 00:50:55,187
Do-do-do-do-do-do-do-do-do-do...

1420
00:50:55,220 --> 00:50:56,588
There have been
no further reports

1421
00:50:56,622 --> 00:50:57,855
of bombing from the west coast.

1422
00:50:57,888 --> 00:51:01,727
But an unconfirmed
report maintains...

1423
00:51:01,760 --> 00:51:02,893
Gentlemen,

1424
00:51:02,927 --> 00:51:05,830
we just smashed his
largest A-bomb plant.

1425
00:51:05,863 --> 00:51:07,798
The next bomb, Oregon.

1426
00:51:07,832 --> 00:51:10,968
Our B-36 has reached target
at 2300.

1427
00:51:11,002 --> 00:51:11,870
CROW: It was closed.

1428
00:51:11,903 --> 00:51:13,805
They blew a hole
right through the middle

1429
00:51:13,838 --> 00:51:14,840
of his plant.

1430
00:51:14,873 --> 00:51:16,373
How many workers there?

1431
00:51:16,407 --> 00:51:17,642
MAN: About 50,000.

1432
00:51:17,675 --> 00:51:19,577
How many casualties
would you estimate there?

1433
00:51:19,610 --> 00:51:21,713
-SERVO: Oh, a lot.
-...say at least half of them.

1434
00:51:21,747 --> 00:51:24,783
Well, what will happen
if he hits New York, Chicago,

1435
00:51:24,817 --> 00:51:25,583
the way we hit him?

1436
00:51:25,617 --> 00:51:26,985
CROW: Can't you just be happy?

1437
00:51:27,018 --> 00:51:28,620
It'd be tough.

1438
00:51:28,653 --> 00:51:30,488
MIKE: Your son drew
another giraffe, sir.

1439
00:51:30,522 --> 00:51:33,558
He's landed paratroops
in California.

1440
00:51:33,592 --> 00:51:34,960
The enemy is dropping
parachute troops

1441
00:51:34,993 --> 00:51:36,193
on the outskirts of the city.

1442
00:51:36,227 --> 00:51:37,528
The Army needs these tanks.

1443
00:51:37,562 --> 00:51:39,965
We got to get on them,
repair them, and do them fast.

1444
00:51:39,998 --> 00:51:41,667
What about the tractors
on the production line?

1445
00:51:41,700 --> 00:51:44,202
Oh, get them out of the road,
dump them in the bay, anything.

1446
00:51:44,235 --> 00:51:45,303
Let me emphasize
that it's touch and go

1447
00:51:45,337 --> 00:51:46,738
whether we can hold the city.

1448
00:51:46,772 --> 00:51:49,173
A dozen tanks one way or another
can make all the difference.

1449
00:51:49,207 --> 00:51:50,275
We'll get them ready fast.

1450
00:51:50,308 --> 00:51:52,043
Tell the men they're on a
24-hour shift

1451
00:51:52,077 --> 00:51:53,345
until those tanks are repaired.

1452
00:51:53,378 --> 00:51:55,480
A 24-hour shift for what?

1453
00:51:55,513 --> 00:51:57,982
To make more money for you?

1454
00:51:58,015 --> 00:52:00,185
We don't have to work
for this rat anymore.

1455
00:52:00,218 --> 00:52:01,285
He's finished.

1456
00:52:01,318 --> 00:52:03,222
All the capitalist rats
are finished.

1457
00:52:03,255 --> 00:52:04,555
Why don't you drop dead?

1458
00:52:04,588 --> 00:52:06,023
Why does he want to make tanks?

1459
00:52:06,057 --> 00:52:07,625
SERVO: Rick, save me.

1460
00:52:07,658 --> 00:52:09,493
When he could make
more money building tractors,

1461
00:52:09,527 --> 00:52:10,562
he build tractors.

1462
00:52:10,595 --> 00:52:13,298
SERVO: What are you,
County-- oh, wow.

1463
00:52:13,332 --> 00:52:14,698
Up, up with hands-- up.

1464
00:52:14,732 --> 00:52:16,100
SERVO: Tractor Police,
John Deere Squad.

1465
00:52:16,133 --> 00:52:17,468
Ah, you are here.

1466
00:52:17,502 --> 00:52:19,070
Just in time.

1467
00:52:19,103 --> 00:52:20,272
I'm in charge here now.

1468
00:52:20,305 --> 00:52:22,173
-SERVO: Aye.
-You were right.

1469
00:52:22,207 --> 00:52:24,142
Your men will work
a 24-hour shift

1470
00:52:24,175 --> 00:52:25,777
until the tanks are repaired,

1471
00:52:25,810 --> 00:52:28,713
but it is the people's army
who will use them.

1472
00:52:28,747 --> 00:52:30,182
[ Gunshots ]

1473
00:52:30,215 --> 00:52:32,450
SERVO: This is
for Alice Chalmers.

1474
00:52:32,483 --> 00:52:34,518
Take on the job,
you will get your order.

1475
00:52:34,552 --> 00:52:35,587
CROW: Hi, I miss anything?

1476
00:52:35,620 --> 00:52:38,557
-SERVO: Oh, whoop.
-Ooh.

1477
00:52:38,590 --> 00:52:42,093
CROW: Let me get two
15-minute break-- oh.

1478
00:52:42,127 --> 00:52:45,030
When middle managers rebel.

1479
00:52:45,063 --> 00:52:46,665
SERVO: Ugh.
Gonna need a new shift super.

1480
00:52:46,698 --> 00:52:49,400
Why do people like you always
think you can beat anybody

1481
00:52:49,433 --> 00:52:50,502
with your bare hands?

1482
00:52:50,535 --> 00:52:51,770
MIKE:
That's an interesting question.

1483
00:52:51,803 --> 00:52:53,905
-And I think to...
-I have my life to live for...

1484
00:52:53,938 --> 00:52:56,307
You would build tanks
in this factory.

1485
00:52:56,340 --> 00:52:57,942
CROW:
Don't finish sentences for me.

1486
00:52:57,975 --> 00:53:00,278
You still have time.

1487
00:53:00,312 --> 00:53:02,647
Only you will build them for us.

1488
00:53:02,680 --> 00:53:04,415
-That's what you think.
-Shut up.

1489
00:53:04,448 --> 00:53:06,450
CROW:
I just wanna build tractors.

1490
00:53:06,483 --> 00:53:08,253
[ Crying ]

1491
00:53:08,287 --> 00:53:10,422
But my orders
are to keep you alive.

1492
00:53:10,455 --> 00:53:12,057
MIKE: So are you gonna finish
the windows?

1493
00:53:12,090 --> 00:53:13,792
We need this factory, you see.

1494
00:53:13,825 --> 00:53:17,362
And you know how to run it
better than anybody else.

1495
00:53:17,395 --> 00:53:20,398
So, there is only one
thing to do.

1496
00:53:20,432 --> 00:53:21,667
You are so dead right.

1497
00:53:21,700 --> 00:53:23,302
SERVO: Little man,
I think I love you.

1498
00:53:23,335 --> 00:53:25,003
I'm just a man who can do it.

1499
00:53:25,037 --> 00:53:27,072
[ Music playing ]

1500
00:53:27,105 --> 00:53:27,938
CROW: Oh.

1501
00:53:27,972 --> 00:53:28,773
[ Gunshots ]

1502
00:53:28,807 --> 00:53:29,473
[ Screams ]

1503
00:53:29,507 --> 00:53:32,610
MIKE: Boy, he almost made it.

1504
00:53:32,643 --> 00:53:34,678
CROW: Okay, I'm dead.
Fine.

1505
00:53:34,712 --> 00:53:36,582
Killer day at the office.

1506
00:53:36,615 --> 00:53:39,117
San Francisco fell
at 12:00 today,

1507
00:53:39,150 --> 00:53:41,252
and the invaders have
established a firm foothold

1508
00:53:41,285 --> 00:53:42,953
on American soil.

1509
00:53:42,987 --> 00:53:44,923
Our military air bases
within fighter plane range

1510
00:53:44,957 --> 00:53:47,392
of Northern California have
been knocked out by A-bombs.

1511
00:53:47,425 --> 00:53:48,827
MIKE:
That's my boyfriend you know.

1512
00:53:48,860 --> 00:53:50,728
...that the Army is being
withdrawn to a defense line

1513
00:53:50,762 --> 00:53:53,398
along the Western borders
of the Rocky Mountains.

1514
00:53:53,432 --> 00:53:55,233
SERVO: Knock it off over there!

1515
00:53:55,267 --> 00:53:56,935
CROW: Ding.

1516
00:53:56,968 --> 00:53:59,370
We now switch controls
to Washington, D.C.

1517
00:53:59,403 --> 00:54:00,905
for an official message.

1518
00:54:00,938 --> 00:54:02,040
CROW: [ Laughing ]

1519
00:54:02,073 --> 00:54:02,873
Hi, kids.

1520
00:54:02,907 --> 00:54:03,975
[ Laughing ]

1521
00:54:04,008 --> 00:54:05,243
SERVO: Oh.

1522
00:54:05,277 --> 00:54:08,280
MAN: Despite a heroic effort
by our Armed Forces...

1523
00:54:08,313 --> 00:54:09,747
SERVO: Bozo has been cancelled.

1524
00:54:09,780 --> 00:54:13,385
MAN: ...the enemy invaders
have now secured San Francisco,

1525
00:54:13,418 --> 00:54:14,618
Oakland,

1526
00:54:14,652 --> 00:54:16,855
Astoria, Oregon,

1527
00:54:16,888 --> 00:54:20,258
-and Port Townsend.
-CROW: And Cucamonga.

1528
00:54:20,292 --> 00:54:23,295
MAN: To the people of these
cities I bring this message.

1529
00:54:23,328 --> 00:54:25,030
SERVO: You're on your own.

1530
00:54:25,063 --> 00:54:26,530
MAN: Do not despair.

1531
00:54:26,563 --> 00:54:28,265
CROW: For those of you
not flash-fried.

1532
00:54:28,300 --> 00:54:29,600
MAN: At 10:00 this morning,

1533
00:54:29,633 --> 00:54:32,670
England and France
declared war on our side.

1534
00:54:32,703 --> 00:54:34,238
SERVO: France has pledge crêpes.

1535
00:54:34,272 --> 00:54:37,975
MAN: All the nations
included in the Atlantic pact

1536
00:54:38,008 --> 00:54:40,378
have risen to defend
the free world.

1537
00:54:40,412 --> 00:54:42,080
CROW:
With strongly worded cables,

1538
00:54:42,113 --> 00:54:43,882
they're very put out.

1539
00:54:43,915 --> 00:54:45,717
MAN: Despite the unprovoked
nature of the attack,

1540
00:54:45,750 --> 00:54:47,752
the war has not been
as one-sided

1541
00:54:47,785 --> 00:54:49,487
as it may now seem to you.

1542
00:54:49,520 --> 00:54:50,888
SERVO: I will now read
The Velveteen Rabbit.

1543
00:54:50,922 --> 00:54:53,692
MAN: For every atom bomb
dropped on our country,

1544
00:54:53,725 --> 00:54:56,460
we have taken three
to the enemy's heartland.

1545
00:54:56,493 --> 00:54:57,995
SERVO: Whoo.

1546
00:54:58,028 --> 00:55:01,532
MAN: And we have huge stocks
of atomic weapons in reserve.

1547
00:55:01,565 --> 00:55:03,100
CROW: Everything must go.

1548
00:55:03,133 --> 00:55:04,268
MAN: Stocks large enough

1549
00:55:04,302 --> 00:55:07,705
to eventually crush the enemy
on his native soil.

1550
00:55:07,738 --> 00:55:09,240
MIKE: He's always bragging
about his huge stocks.

1551
00:55:09,273 --> 00:55:11,542
MAN: And end forever his power
to make war

1552
00:55:11,575 --> 00:55:14,478
on any nation anywhere.

1553
00:55:14,512 --> 00:55:15,680
So be of good courage.

1554
00:55:15,713 --> 00:55:17,115
SERVO: I think Peggy Noonan
wrote the speech.

1555
00:55:17,148 --> 00:55:20,852
MAN: For we have met
the first shock of aggression,

1556
00:55:20,885 --> 00:55:23,855
and we have returned
blow for blow.

1557
00:55:23,888 --> 00:55:25,390
CROW: And that boy's name

1558
00:55:25,423 --> 00:55:26,457
was Raymond Burr.

1559
00:55:26,490 --> 00:55:27,925
MAN: And even as I
speak to you,

1560
00:55:27,958 --> 00:55:28,727
CROW: I'm not wearing pants.

1561
00:55:28,760 --> 00:55:29,993
MAN: our Pacific fleet

1562
00:55:30,028 --> 00:55:33,965
is carrying the conflict
to the enemy's homeland.

1563
00:55:33,998 --> 00:55:37,202
SERVO: But first,
victory at sea.

1564
00:55:37,235 --> 00:55:40,038
[ Cannon fire ]

1565
00:55:40,072 --> 00:55:42,473
Excuse me, are you
the enemy's homeland?

1566
00:55:42,507 --> 00:55:46,845
[ Cannon fire continues ]

1567
00:55:46,878 --> 00:55:48,613
MIKE: We're destroying
their beach resorts

1568
00:55:48,647 --> 00:55:50,982
and vacation areas.

1569
00:55:51,015 --> 00:55:54,818
CROW: Another senseless
fly-by shooting.

1570
00:55:54,852 --> 00:55:59,957
SERVO: The Dean Martin-
Jerry Lewis feud is heating up.

1571
00:56:00,023 --> 00:56:01,760
I wish they'd go back
to that president's speech.

1572
00:56:01,827 --> 00:56:03,260
That was a lot more fascinating.

1573
00:56:03,327 --> 00:56:04,362
CROW:
Yeah, that was great.

1574
00:56:04,428 --> 00:56:05,830
SERVO: Remember
that president's speech?

1575
00:56:05,830 --> 00:56:08,467
CROW: Oh, how can I forget?

1576
00:56:08,533 --> 00:56:09,533
Loved it.

1577
00:56:09,567 --> 00:56:11,837
[ Gunshots ]

1578
00:56:11,837 --> 00:56:14,972
SERVO: Oh, not Levittown, no!

1579
00:56:15,005 --> 00:56:17,675
-MIKE: Not the hog barn!
-SERVO: Please.

1580
00:56:17,708 --> 00:56:20,043
[ Gunshots ]

1581
00:56:20,078 --> 00:56:22,613
CROW:
They bomb our nation's hobos.

1582
00:56:22,647 --> 00:56:24,715
SERVO: They took out
Boxcar Willie.

1583
00:56:24,748 --> 00:56:26,350
[ Gunfire, explosion ]

1584
00:56:26,383 --> 00:56:28,853
Ooh.

1585
00:56:28,887 --> 00:56:31,588
MIKE: Come on, aren't they
overreacting just a bit?

1586
00:56:31,622 --> 00:56:33,925
SERVO: I think someone's
heated up here.

1587
00:56:33,958 --> 00:56:36,560
CROW: The Carnival Cruise Line
fights back.

1588
00:56:36,593 --> 00:56:40,465
♪ If you could see me die. ♪

1589
00:56:40,498 --> 00:56:41,767
SERVO: Wait, these many bombs?

1590
00:56:41,800 --> 00:56:43,333
Must be a comedy club.

1591
00:56:43,367 --> 00:56:45,537
ALL: [ Laughs ]

1592
00:56:45,570 --> 00:56:47,705
MIKE: Do they have to follow
the freeway when they're flying?

1593
00:56:47,738 --> 00:56:48,773
SERVO: I guess.

1594
00:56:48,807 --> 00:56:50,808
CROW: The freeway
to the danger zone.

1595
00:56:50,842 --> 00:56:53,612
So, World War III is gonna be
a lot like World War II.

1596
00:56:53,645 --> 00:56:55,213
-SERVO: Looks like.
-MIKE: Mm-hmm.

1597
00:56:55,247 --> 00:56:58,148
CROW: Similar design.

1598
00:56:58,182 --> 00:57:00,017
SERVO: Ratatat-tat.

1599
00:57:00,050 --> 00:57:04,722
Ratatat-tat.

1600
00:57:04,755 --> 00:57:07,492
MIKE: No, I can't swim.
I have tubes in my ears.

1601
00:57:07,525 --> 00:57:12,663
SERVO: Hey.

1602
00:57:12,697 --> 00:57:14,132
I'm fine, just a little dizzy.

1603
00:57:14,165 --> 00:57:19,103
No problem,
I've got it under control.

1604
00:57:19,137 --> 00:57:25,843
[ Music playing ]

1605
00:57:25,877 --> 00:57:31,582
CROW: And I'll just put
your arm back on.

1606
00:57:31,615 --> 00:57:32,683
MIKE: Mount Man.

1607
00:57:32,717 --> 00:57:34,285
-SERVO: [ Chuckles ]
-How do you feel?

1608
00:57:34,318 --> 00:57:35,653
I feel great.

1609
00:57:35,687 --> 00:57:37,688
How much of the red stuff
did you take out?

1610
00:57:37,722 --> 00:57:39,057
Just a pint.

1611
00:57:39,090 --> 00:57:40,958
The next time
I'll give you a fifth.

1612
00:57:40,992 --> 00:57:42,927
All right, come around
in about 12 weeks.

1613
00:57:42,960 --> 00:57:45,597
CROW: I only hear that joke
about eight million times a day.

1614
00:57:45,630 --> 00:57:46,630
MAN: Hi, honey.

1615
00:57:46,663 --> 00:57:47,932
FEMALE: Hey,
what are you doing here?

1616
00:57:47,965 --> 00:57:50,202
Oh, I thought I'd spare you
a few red corpuscles.

1617
00:57:50,235 --> 00:57:51,468
-Swell.
-SERVO: War's been a boon

1618
00:57:51,502 --> 00:57:52,537
to this guy.

1619
00:57:52,570 --> 00:57:54,405
Tried to join
the Air Force today...

1620
00:57:54,438 --> 00:57:56,207
CROW: Tried to join as a WAC.

1621
00:57:56,240 --> 00:57:58,375
Ninety thousand guys
are trying to join now

1622
00:57:58,408 --> 00:58:00,612
that it's too late to train men.

1623
00:58:00,645 --> 00:58:01,745
What they need is equipment.

1624
00:58:01,778 --> 00:58:02,913
What we need is blood.

1625
00:58:02,947 --> 00:58:06,183
MIKE: Well, take all of his.

1626
00:58:06,217 --> 00:58:07,952
MAN: You sure you know
what you're doing, huh?

1627
00:58:07,985 --> 00:58:09,220
-CARLA: Please.
-SERVO: But now that you

1628
00:58:09,253 --> 00:58:10,722
mention it,
I do have no idea.

1629
00:58:10,755 --> 00:58:12,390
-It's cold.
-Don't be such a sissy.

1630
00:58:12,423 --> 00:58:15,493
CROW: Did you ever see
The World According to Garp?

1631
00:58:15,527 --> 00:58:20,532
SERVO: Ow, ow, oh.

1632
00:58:20,565 --> 00:58:23,233
-Make a fist.
-Okay.

1633
00:58:23,267 --> 00:58:25,337
-You know you're beautiful?
-CROW: Yes, I know.

1634
00:58:25,370 --> 00:58:26,938
We're ready.

1635
00:58:26,972 --> 00:58:28,707
Does she know what she's doing
with that thing?

1636
00:58:28,740 --> 00:58:30,140
-You can trust her.
-Yeah, I don't trust--

1637
00:58:30,173 --> 00:58:31,475
I trust you, I don't trust...

1638
00:58:31,508 --> 00:58:33,712
CROW: Because she had thing
and I was with the thing.

1639
00:58:33,745 --> 00:58:35,713
SERVO: [ Laughing ]

1640
00:58:35,747 --> 00:58:37,648
MIKE: He has no blood.
There's no blood in him.

1641
00:58:37,682 --> 00:58:38,983
He has...

1642
00:58:39,017 --> 00:58:40,752
CROW: Man, I really like cattle.

1643
00:58:40,785 --> 00:58:41,887
MAN: All over America,

1644
00:58:41,920 --> 00:58:43,988
long lines are forming
in front of

1645
00:58:44,022 --> 00:58:45,557
Red Cross Blood Bank
centers,

1646
00:58:45,590 --> 00:58:48,525
but authorities estimate
that another five million pints

1647
00:58:48,560 --> 00:58:50,060
are needed immediately.

1648
00:58:50,093 --> 00:58:51,997
Even more if they ramp up
bomb attacks

1649
00:58:52,030 --> 00:58:53,598
on the major centers
of population.

1650
00:58:53,632 --> 00:58:55,065
SERVO: Oh, I'm sorry.

1651
00:58:55,098 --> 00:58:57,135
I didn't mean you look exactly
like Linda Hunt.

1652
00:58:57,168 --> 00:58:59,303
Gosh, it's sure great to talk
to my kids

1653
00:58:59,337 --> 00:59:01,338
from Boulder City.

1654
00:59:01,372 --> 00:59:03,307
Take the first turn
to the right.

1655
00:59:03,340 --> 00:59:04,742
Not far to go, huh?

1656
00:59:04,775 --> 00:59:06,010
We'll be home in 10 minutes.

1657
00:59:06,043 --> 00:59:08,178
You'll be home, brother, not me.

1658
00:59:08,212 --> 00:59:10,147
They got a new flag
over my home.

1659
00:59:10,180 --> 00:59:11,415
SERVO: Whoo.

1660
00:59:11,448 --> 00:59:12,617
That's too bad.

1661
00:59:12,650 --> 00:59:13,852
CROW: But just drive, okay?

1662
00:59:13,885 --> 00:59:15,520
Got any family
in San Francisco?

1663
00:59:15,553 --> 00:59:17,222
Just me and the cab.

1664
00:59:17,255 --> 00:59:19,490
I'll give the two of you
a job on my ranch.

1665
00:59:19,523 --> 00:59:20,325
Oh, thanks.

1666
00:59:20,358 --> 00:59:21,758
SERVO: And there's
an airport fee,

1667
00:59:21,792 --> 00:59:23,728
you know that, right?

1668
00:59:23,762 --> 00:59:26,063
Look at those bombers.

1669
00:59:26,097 --> 00:59:27,832
I'm sure glad
we've got a lot of them.

1670
00:59:27,865 --> 00:59:28,867
You said it.

1671
00:59:28,900 --> 00:59:30,033
SERVO: Mm-hmm.

1672
00:59:30,067 --> 00:59:30,802
Huh?

1673
00:59:30,835 --> 00:59:32,337
Jet bombers with
swept-back wings.

1674
00:59:32,370 --> 00:59:33,403
I got you.

1675
00:59:33,437 --> 00:59:35,640
We just intercepted a jet
attack headed this way.

1676
00:59:35,673 --> 00:59:37,275
They think maybe
the dam's a target.

1677
00:59:37,308 --> 00:59:39,410
How many planes?
How far away?

1678
00:59:39,443 --> 00:59:40,978
How many planes?

1679
00:59:41,012 --> 00:59:42,280
-I got you.
-SERVO: How far away?

1680
00:59:42,313 --> 00:59:44,148
Last seen at six C for Charlie.

1681
00:59:44,182 --> 00:59:46,083
-SERVO: You just talk to him.
-About a dozen jets,

1682
00:59:46,117 --> 00:59:47,318
120 miles west of here.

1683
00:59:47,352 --> 00:59:49,353
They about shot down
most of them.

1684
00:59:49,387 --> 00:59:51,455
SERVO: Oops,
stock footage at 3:00.

1685
00:59:51,488 --> 00:59:52,790
What's that?

1686
00:59:52,823 --> 00:59:54,825
CROW: Yeah, it's about a dozen
jets heading this way.

1687
00:59:54,858 --> 00:59:57,928
Oh, my God!

1688
00:59:57,962 --> 01:00:00,298
Post 327 to command,
post 327 to command,

1689
01:00:00,332 --> 01:00:02,800
enemy jets approaching,
Boulder Dam.

1690
01:00:02,833 --> 01:00:05,537
Enemy jets approaching
Boulder Dam.

1691
01:00:05,570 --> 01:00:07,238
Enemy planes coming in.

1692
01:00:07,272 --> 01:00:08,538
Open fire.

1693
01:00:08,572 --> 01:00:10,908
SERVO: The Guns of Navarone
versus the Demonic Toys.

1694
01:00:10,942 --> 01:00:14,878
And Dollman is there.

1695
01:00:14,912 --> 01:00:19,650
CROW: Don't let them
get to the gift shop.

1696
01:00:19,683 --> 01:00:22,220
MIKE: If you shoot them down,
you just have to clean them up.

1697
01:00:22,253 --> 01:00:24,355
SERVO: This makes me pine
for Red Dawn.

1698
01:00:24,388 --> 01:00:25,288
CROW: Avenge me.

1699
01:00:25,323 --> 01:00:28,058
-Avenge me.
-Three jets attacking dam.

1700
01:00:28,092 --> 01:00:31,128
MIKE: I mean, darn, excuse me.

1701
01:00:31,162 --> 01:00:36,367
SERVO: Launch cargo.

1702
01:00:36,400 --> 01:00:38,535
MIKE: Just realized
the president's approval rating

1703
01:00:38,568 --> 01:00:42,940
must be plummeting.

1704
01:00:42,973 --> 01:00:47,512
CROW: How do I not dive anymore?

1705
01:00:47,545 --> 01:00:49,080
SERVO: Whoa, whoa, whoa.

1706
01:00:49,113 --> 01:00:51,115
Hey, those zooms are deadly.

1707
01:00:51,148 --> 01:00:52,017
Wow.

1708
01:00:52,050 --> 01:00:57,455
MIKE:
Vince Coleman's final revenge.

1709
01:00:57,488 --> 01:01:03,593
CROW: Despite the best efforts
of the little Dutch boy...

1710
01:01:03,627 --> 01:01:05,262
[ Explosion ]

1711
01:01:05,295 --> 01:01:07,232
Sounded like something
blew up.

1712
01:01:07,265 --> 01:01:08,398
MAN: Emergency announcement.

1713
01:01:08,432 --> 01:01:10,402
Enemy planes are attacking
Boulder Dam.

1714
01:01:10,435 --> 01:01:12,970
I repeat, enemy planes
are attacking Boulder Dam.

1715
01:01:13,003 --> 01:01:14,772
CROW: Good thing I brought
the motorman's helper.

1716
01:01:14,805 --> 01:01:16,407
MAN: The dam's...

1717
01:01:16,440 --> 01:01:19,077
MAN: Attention, all citizens,
Boulder Dam has been destroyed

1718
01:01:19,110 --> 01:01:20,343
by enemy actions.

1719
01:01:20,378 --> 01:01:22,613
Evacuate all low ground
immediately.

1720
01:01:22,647 --> 01:01:24,348
Attention, all citizens.

1721
01:01:24,382 --> 01:01:26,250
Step on it,
we got to get to my family.

1722
01:01:26,283 --> 01:01:28,318
MIKE: This guy's gonna be
so mad when he finds out

1723
01:01:28,352 --> 01:01:30,855
there's an express bus
he could've taken.

1724
01:01:30,888 --> 01:01:34,025
[ Music playing ]

1725
01:01:34,058 --> 01:01:35,927
CROW: Sir,
you're up to about $11,000,

1726
01:01:35,960 --> 01:01:40,330
sure you don't want me
to drop you off?

1727
01:01:40,363 --> 01:01:41,965
Look at that.

1728
01:01:41,998 --> 01:01:44,202
SERVO: Gee, Central Casting
sent over a family.

1729
01:01:44,235 --> 01:01:45,437
Daddy!

1730
01:01:45,470 --> 01:01:46,570
MAN: The dam's out.

1731
01:01:46,603 --> 01:01:48,005
-WOMAN: The dam?
-MAN: Yes, they bombed it.

1732
01:01:48,038 --> 01:01:50,007
Boulder Dam.
Get in, quick, hurry.

1733
01:01:50,040 --> 01:01:54,312
MIKE: Oh, great to see you
too, honey.

1734
01:01:54,345 --> 01:01:56,280
♪ Up through the ground
came a-bubblin' crude ♪

1735
01:01:56,313 --> 01:01:57,582
♪ Water that is ♪

1736
01:01:57,615 --> 01:01:59,717
Water will be a hundred
feet deep here any minute.

1737
01:01:59,750 --> 01:02:01,518
What happened?
What happened?

1738
01:02:01,552 --> 01:02:03,955
Those bombers that just flew
over, they weren't ours.

1739
01:02:03,988 --> 01:02:05,288
Can't you go any faster?

1740
01:02:05,322 --> 01:02:07,057
SERVO: Sure, I'd drive you here
from San Francisco,

1741
01:02:07,092 --> 01:02:08,827
but I guess I am a jerk, huh?

1742
01:02:08,860 --> 01:02:12,397
-Mommy, I'm scared.
-Shh, darling.

1743
01:02:12,430 --> 01:02:14,798
MIKE: Usually when there's a
flood, you can never find a cab.

1744
01:02:14,832 --> 01:02:15,867
Am I right here?

1745
01:02:15,900 --> 01:02:21,838
CROW: We should've got
a Checker cab.

1746
01:02:21,872 --> 01:02:23,607
SERVO: [ Humming ]

1747
01:02:23,640 --> 01:02:27,545
-Hank, oh.
-Faster, faster.

1748
01:02:27,578 --> 01:02:32,383
SERVO: Oh, guess the water
knew a shortcut, huh?

1749
01:02:32,450 --> 01:02:33,952
[ Screaming ]

1750
01:02:33,985 --> 01:02:35,653
-SERVO: Oh.
-MIKE: I knew I'd get soaked

1751
01:02:35,687 --> 01:02:38,990
for this cab ride.

1752
01:02:39,057 --> 01:02:43,493
SERVO: The meter
is still running, pal.

1753
01:02:43,560 --> 01:02:46,563
Oh, ironically he always used
to leave his hat in cabs.

1754
01:02:46,597 --> 01:02:47,598
CROW: Hmm, sad.

1755
01:02:47,665 --> 01:02:49,433
-MIKE: Oh, look at this.
-SERVO: Oh, my God.

1756
01:02:49,467 --> 01:02:51,002
MIKE: Boy, when
that doll wets...

1757
01:02:51,035 --> 01:02:53,203
[ Chuckles ]

1758
01:02:53,237 --> 01:02:56,373
Destruction of Boulder Dam
by an atomic missile today

1759
01:02:56,407 --> 01:02:59,210
was only the culminating
disaster in what will go down

1760
01:02:59,243 --> 01:03:01,145
in history as Black Friday

1761
01:03:01,178 --> 01:03:02,280
for the United States
of America.

1762
01:03:02,313 --> 01:03:03,915
CROW: Or freaky Friday.

1763
01:03:03,948 --> 01:03:07,083
MAN: At 10:27 this morning,
off the coast of California,

1764
01:03:07,117 --> 01:03:08,752
an American warship
was the victim

1765
01:03:08,785 --> 01:03:10,888
of another new atomic weapon,

1766
01:03:10,922 --> 01:03:12,857
when the carrier Crown Point

1767
01:03:12,890 --> 01:03:16,393
suffered a direct hit
by an atomic torpedo,

1768
01:03:16,427 --> 01:03:18,362
first victim of a weapon
that threatens

1769
01:03:18,395 --> 01:03:21,465
the very existence
of the United States fleet.

1770
01:03:21,498 --> 01:03:24,835
The Crown Point waged
a gallant fight for survival

1771
01:03:24,868 --> 01:03:26,403
but at 5:20 this afternoon,

1772
01:03:26,437 --> 01:03:28,472
the fire reached
her boiler room,

1773
01:03:28,505 --> 01:03:31,108
and Capt. Headley gave
the order to abandon ship.

1774
01:03:31,142 --> 01:03:32,677
SERVO: Wise decision, captain.

1775
01:03:32,710 --> 01:03:35,112
MIKE: We told Dom DeLuise
to stand in the middle,

1776
01:03:35,145 --> 01:03:38,582
but I blame this on Exxon.

1777
01:03:38,615 --> 01:03:39,950
Meanwhile,

1778
01:03:39,983 --> 01:03:43,120
flames swept the entire
State of California tonight,

1779
01:03:43,153 --> 01:03:44,555
as the people
of the Pacific Coast

1780
01:03:44,588 --> 01:03:46,023
put their industrial
establishments

1781
01:03:46,057 --> 01:03:47,358
to the torch,

1782
01:03:47,392 --> 01:03:49,793
rather than allow them
to fall into enemy hands.

1783
01:03:49,827 --> 01:03:50,995
SERVO: Oh.

1784
01:03:51,028 --> 01:03:53,030
MAN: Here is a food
warehouse in Oakland...

1785
01:03:53,063 --> 01:03:54,498
MIKE: The chicken's done.

1786
01:03:54,532 --> 01:03:57,368
MAN: ...its owners to keep
the thousands of tons of flour

1787
01:03:57,402 --> 01:04:00,437
and sugar it held from being
used to feed the enemy.

1788
01:04:00,470 --> 01:04:02,072
-SERVO: War and peace.
-MAN: This is Richmond,

1789
01:04:02,105 --> 01:04:04,342
California,
land of western petroleum.

1790
01:04:04,375 --> 01:04:05,977
-CROW: No, it's not.
-MAN: A million gallons

1791
01:04:06,010 --> 01:04:07,778
of high-test airplane gasoline

1792
01:04:07,812 --> 01:04:09,113
go up in flames

1793
01:04:09,147 --> 01:04:11,415
to implement
the Scorched Earth policy

1794
01:04:11,448 --> 01:04:13,617
with which a resolute
civilian population

1795
01:04:13,650 --> 01:04:16,387
is meeting the first invasion
of America

1796
01:04:16,420 --> 01:04:18,388
since the War of 1812.

1797
01:04:18,422 --> 01:04:19,490
MIKE: When was that war?

1798
01:04:19,523 --> 01:04:21,492
MAN: Disaster follows disaster

1799
01:04:21,525 --> 01:04:24,162
as railroad employees
wreck their own trains

1800
01:04:24,195 --> 01:04:25,863
to slow the enemy drive.

1801
01:04:25,897 --> 01:04:26,763
SERVO: Pretty dumb, huh?

1802
01:04:26,797 --> 01:04:27,698
MAN: A steel plant

1803
01:04:27,732 --> 01:04:30,200
built at a cost
of $50 million dollars

1804
01:04:30,233 --> 01:04:31,402
burns to the ground.

1805
01:04:31,435 --> 01:04:33,370
CROW: And Allstate is there.

1806
01:04:33,403 --> 01:04:34,705
One part of the
terrible financial

1807
01:04:34,738 --> 01:04:35,707
balance sheet of war.

1808
01:04:35,740 --> 01:04:37,942
Billions of dollars
of property lost

1809
01:04:37,975 --> 01:04:39,943
to the American people forever

1810
01:04:39,977 --> 01:04:41,212
because we did not provide

1811
01:04:41,245 --> 01:04:43,713
a strong enough army
to protect ourselves.

1812
01:04:43,747 --> 01:04:44,615
SERVO: Aw.

1813
01:04:44,648 --> 01:04:46,817
I heard they got 10,000
transport planes

1814
01:04:46,850 --> 01:04:48,152
flying in soldiers.

1815
01:04:48,185 --> 01:04:50,420
Probably got half a million
men in California by now.

1816
01:04:50,453 --> 01:04:52,155
-SERVO: Well, the...
-Fella I know said his brother

1817
01:04:52,188 --> 01:04:53,623
heard he had better
than 60 ships

1818
01:04:53,657 --> 01:04:55,558
-in the San Francisco Harbor.
-SERVO: You see the problem...

1819
01:04:55,593 --> 01:04:57,193
They landed a couple
of hundred heavy tanks

1820
01:04:57,227 --> 01:04:58,862
and maybe a thousand
atom bombs.

1821
01:04:58,895 --> 01:05:00,397
The way I figure it's this:

1822
01:05:00,430 --> 01:05:02,232
They know they can't
fight all the way

1823
01:05:02,267 --> 01:05:03,433
across the United States.

1824
01:05:03,467 --> 01:05:05,637
You know, this landing's
just a diversion, see?

1825
01:05:05,670 --> 01:05:07,705
I mean, they're just waiting
for us to send

1826
01:05:07,738 --> 01:05:09,240
our whole army out west.

1827
01:05:09,273 --> 01:05:10,775
Then they'll overrun Europe.

1828
01:05:10,808 --> 01:05:13,177
Jesus. That's what they're
after - airplane bases.

1829
01:05:13,210 --> 01:05:15,345
-SERVO: Can't talk to you, too.
-...get them, they'll start

1830
01:05:15,378 --> 01:05:17,415
to bomb Pittsburgh, Detroit,
places like that.

1831
01:05:17,448 --> 01:05:20,450
And we sure bombed the daylights
out of them yesterday.

1832
01:05:20,483 --> 01:05:21,585
Oh, another drink, Tim.

1833
01:05:21,618 --> 01:05:26,090
-CROW: Sure, Mr. Hot.
-Coming right up.

1834
01:05:26,123 --> 01:05:27,358
How about letting me
buy you one?

1835
01:05:27,392 --> 01:05:29,627
MIKE: You come
to this war often?

1836
01:05:29,660 --> 01:05:30,393
No, thanks.

1837
01:05:30,427 --> 01:05:31,628
Might as well have another.

1838
01:05:31,662 --> 01:05:32,797
You know what the fellow says,

1839
01:05:32,830 --> 01:05:34,832
"Drink and be merry,
for tomorrow we die."

1840
01:05:34,865 --> 01:05:37,200
CROW: Not that funny
when it's true, Ed.

1841
01:05:37,233 --> 01:05:38,435
I'd rather not, thanks.

1842
01:05:38,468 --> 01:05:41,905
MIKE: I need more woman friends.

1843
01:05:41,938 --> 01:05:44,275
Well, this war has really put
a spring in my step.

1844
01:05:44,308 --> 01:05:46,310
-Hi, honey.
-Hi.

1845
01:05:46,343 --> 01:05:48,245
-How's the blood bank?
-It's fine.

1846
01:05:48,278 --> 01:05:50,047
And we've got a new record
this week.

1847
01:05:50,080 --> 01:05:52,048
You set a record with me
a long time ago.

1848
01:05:52,082 --> 01:05:53,283
MIKE: God, I'm smooth.
Anyway...

1849
01:05:53,317 --> 01:05:55,352
Give me a beer, Tim, huh?

1850
01:05:55,385 --> 01:05:57,220
Well, they turned me down
again today.

1851
01:05:57,253 --> 01:05:58,355
The Air Force?

1852
01:05:58,388 --> 01:06:00,323
Navy this time.

1853
01:06:00,357 --> 01:06:02,860
Air Force doesn't want me,
army doesn't want me,

1854
01:06:02,893 --> 01:06:03,793
Navy doesn't want me.

1855
01:06:03,827 --> 01:06:06,197
CROW: Apparently,
I'm too good-looking.

1856
01:06:06,230 --> 01:06:08,332
That's the best thing
I've heard today.

1857
01:06:08,365 --> 01:06:11,235
I mean it, too.

1858
01:06:11,268 --> 01:06:13,203
SERVO: You're a Hindu.

1859
01:06:13,237 --> 01:06:14,572
Why wouldn't the Navy take you?

1860
01:06:14,605 --> 01:06:15,840
-Same old story.
-CROW: They're jealous.

1861
01:06:15,873 --> 01:06:17,942
More men than
they have weapons for.

1862
01:06:17,975 --> 01:06:20,678
Soldier is no good without a gun
and a sailor is no good

1863
01:06:20,712 --> 01:06:21,378
without a ship.

1864
01:06:21,412 --> 01:06:23,213
Don't let it get you down, chum.

1865
01:06:23,247 --> 01:06:24,915
Remember old Tim's motto.

1866
01:06:24,948 --> 01:06:26,150
Let Jack do it.

1867
01:06:26,183 --> 01:06:27,918
-Jack?
-CROW: What the hell?

1868
01:06:27,952 --> 01:06:29,520
TIM: George's brother.

1869
01:06:29,553 --> 01:06:31,455
MIKE: Well, the whole George
thing just isn't that funny.

1870
01:06:31,488 --> 01:06:33,657
Oh, you're killing me.

1871
01:06:33,690 --> 01:06:37,127
CROW: You set a record with my--
oh, yeah, used that, hmm?

1872
01:06:37,160 --> 01:06:39,730
-Right now?
-Right now.

1873
01:06:39,763 --> 01:06:41,732
I'm with you.

1874
01:06:41,765 --> 01:06:44,435
CROW: And I'll be back
for you later, Timmy.

1875
01:06:44,468 --> 01:06:47,303
TIM: Hey, Vince.
You forgot your beer.

1876
01:06:47,337 --> 01:06:49,440
-You drink it.
-SERVO: I don't drink this

1877
01:06:49,473 --> 01:06:51,742
-swill...
-Yeah.

1878
01:06:51,775 --> 01:06:54,678
[ Glugs ]

1879
01:06:54,712 --> 01:06:56,180
[ Laughs ]

1880
01:06:56,213 --> 01:06:57,448
MIKE: He's got cirrhosis
of the liver.

1881
01:06:57,482 --> 01:06:58,682
Tim, you're a character.

1882
01:06:58,715 --> 01:07:00,885
What are you gonna do now
that there's a war on?

1883
01:07:00,918 --> 01:07:04,388
Same thing I did
in the last couple of wars.

1884
01:07:04,422 --> 01:07:05,823
Shake daiquiris.

1885
01:07:05,857 --> 01:07:06,923
SERVO: I'm a patriot.

1886
01:07:06,957 --> 01:07:09,627
CROW: You should do comedy.
You're just so funny.

1887
01:07:09,660 --> 01:07:10,460
[ Laughs ]

1888
01:07:10,493 --> 01:07:11,662
MAN:
Emergency announcement.

1889
01:07:11,695 --> 01:07:13,463
-SERVO: Hmm?
-Radar screens have picked up

1890
01:07:13,497 --> 01:07:15,498
unidentified aircraft
approaching New York.

1891
01:07:15,532 --> 01:07:17,367
-SERVO: Radar.
-The red alert is on.

1892
01:07:17,402 --> 01:07:19,803
I repeat,
emergency announcement.

1893
01:07:19,837 --> 01:07:22,573
Unidentified planes
approaching New York.

1894
01:07:22,607 --> 01:07:24,175
The red alert is on.

1895
01:07:24,208 --> 01:07:25,608
CROW: Patty's in trouble again.

1896
01:07:25,642 --> 01:07:28,212
You suppose they're really
going to bomb New York?

1897
01:07:28,245 --> 01:07:29,447
They threatened to.

1898
01:07:29,480 --> 01:07:31,382
It was on the newswire.

1899
01:07:31,415 --> 01:07:33,417
We didn't wanna release it
and start a panic.

1900
01:07:33,450 --> 01:07:35,385
SERVO: We thought it would
make a nice surprise.

1901
01:07:35,418 --> 01:07:37,220
I'm not afraid.

1902
01:07:37,253 --> 01:07:38,588
I'm not afraid at all.

1903
01:07:38,622 --> 01:07:39,823
SERVO: Neither am I, let's go.

1904
01:07:39,857 --> 01:07:44,628
-MIKE: Yeah.
-CROW: This is our war.

1905
01:07:44,662 --> 01:07:46,697
Carla, there may not be
much time left,

1906
01:07:46,730 --> 01:07:49,400
but in the few days there are,
I want to spend it with you.

1907
01:07:49,433 --> 01:07:51,035
I want that, too.

1908
01:07:51,068 --> 01:08:02,245
[ Doors closing ]

1909
01:08:02,278 --> 01:08:07,685
-I am Mr. Jenga.
-Jenga, Jenga, Jenga.

1910
01:08:07,718 --> 01:08:09,085
-Hey, I win again.
-Hey.

1911
01:08:09,120 --> 01:08:10,553
SERVO: What's so hard
about this game, anyway?

1912
01:08:10,587 --> 01:08:11,788
MIKE: Servo,
that's not the point.

1913
01:08:11,822 --> 01:08:13,123
SERVO: Then, what is the point?

1914
01:08:13,157 --> 01:08:15,292
[ Indistinct chatter ]

1915
01:08:15,325 --> 01:08:17,928
BOMB: Hey, hiya.

1916
01:08:17,962 --> 01:08:19,062
-Hi.
-Hey, Mike.

1917
01:08:19,095 --> 01:08:20,330
It looks like some kind of bomb.

1918
01:08:20,363 --> 01:08:22,432
Some kind of bomb?

1919
01:08:22,467 --> 01:08:24,202
I'm the bomb, kid!

1920
01:08:24,235 --> 01:08:27,170
I'm it, Mr. A1-Armageddon-

1921
01:08:27,203 --> 01:08:29,607
Duck-and-Cover-end-of-the-world-

1922
01:08:29,640 --> 01:08:32,308
flesh-melting-atom-bomb.

1923
01:08:32,342 --> 01:08:33,543
Wow.

1924
01:08:33,577 --> 01:08:36,147
But you can call me Bomb.

1925
01:08:36,180 --> 01:08:37,413
MIKE: Why so glum, Bomb?

1926
01:08:37,447 --> 01:08:39,650
You're looking
at a dinosaur, kid.

1927
01:08:39,683 --> 01:08:42,318
I could remember the salad days,

1928
01:08:42,352 --> 01:08:43,853
lounging in the belly

1929
01:08:43,887 --> 01:08:45,588
of the B-52,

1930
01:08:45,622 --> 01:08:46,990
cruising up and down

1931
01:08:47,023 --> 01:08:49,593
the coast of Yakutsk.

1932
01:08:49,627 --> 01:08:52,128
I meant something, then.

1933
01:08:52,162 --> 01:08:53,263
Hey, Lenny,

1934
01:08:53,297 --> 01:08:55,833
how about another
Manhattan project,

1935
01:08:55,867 --> 01:08:57,502
put it on my tab?

1936
01:08:57,535 --> 01:08:59,170
You probably don't even remember

1937
01:08:59,203 --> 01:09:01,338
the Cuban missile crisis.

1938
01:09:01,372 --> 01:09:02,438
MIKE: Well, I, you know...

1939
01:09:02,472 --> 01:09:03,673
Let me tell you something.

1940
01:09:03,707 --> 01:09:06,110
Bombs don't kill people.

1941
01:09:06,177 --> 01:09:08,378
Well, I guess maybe they do,
but the point is,

1942
01:09:08,378 --> 01:09:10,513
I can be used
for good things, too.

1943
01:09:10,580 --> 01:09:13,083
You want a big stinking hole
in the ground?

1944
01:09:13,117 --> 01:09:14,385
I'm your man.

1945
01:09:14,385 --> 01:09:15,518
Should you really be smoking?

1946
01:09:15,585 --> 01:09:18,288
Oh, the crap I take from these

1947
01:09:18,288 --> 01:09:20,390
sandal-wearing burnouts.

1948
01:09:20,390 --> 01:09:23,460
You can't help a kid
with nuclear arms.

1949
01:09:23,493 --> 01:09:26,163
Oh, yeah.
What do you call these, huh?

1950
01:09:26,197 --> 01:09:27,965
Oh,

1951
01:09:27,998 --> 01:09:29,333
I better mellow out.

1952
01:09:29,367 --> 01:09:32,102
Core temperature
is starting to heat up.

1953
01:09:32,135 --> 01:09:33,137
Yeah.

1954
01:09:33,170 --> 01:09:34,438
Well, I feel kind of funny.

1955
01:09:34,472 --> 01:09:36,273
I-- boom.

1956
01:09:36,307 --> 01:09:37,542
[ Screams ]

1957
01:09:37,575 --> 01:09:39,577
I'm just kidding, guys.

1958
01:09:39,610 --> 01:09:40,677
-Oh, be careful.
-Geez.

1959
01:09:40,710 --> 01:09:42,278
It can't be that bad, Mr. Bomb.

1960
01:09:42,312 --> 01:09:43,913
Things are looking up.

1961
01:09:43,947 --> 01:09:45,415
Take North Korea, for instance.

1962
01:09:45,448 --> 01:09:46,983
Oh, yeah, the instability
in Eastern Europe.

1963
01:09:47,017 --> 01:09:48,585
-Yeah.
-There's always a despotic

1964
01:09:48,618 --> 01:09:51,088
dictator or two looking
for Mr. Good Bomb.

1965
01:09:51,122 --> 01:09:52,088
-Sure.
-Yeah.

1966
01:09:52,122 --> 01:09:53,190
That's right.

1967
01:09:53,223 --> 01:09:54,825
You got a point there, you know?

1968
01:09:54,858 --> 01:09:57,527
I guess things
ain't so bad, after all.

1969
01:09:57,562 --> 01:09:59,263
Yeah, I feel better already.

1970
01:09:59,297 --> 01:10:00,998
-Thanks, guys.
-Yeah. sure.

1971
01:10:01,032 --> 01:10:04,235
I think I'll go call
that weasel Helen Caldicott up

1972
01:10:04,268 --> 01:10:08,138
I like to breathe real heavy
and then hang up.

1973
01:10:08,172 --> 01:10:09,038
She knows.

1974
01:10:09,072 --> 01:10:09,707
[ Laughs ]

1975
01:10:09,740 --> 01:10:11,342
Hey, thanks again.

1976
01:10:11,375 --> 01:10:12,208
See you.

1977
01:10:12,242 --> 01:10:14,043
-Okay, no problem.
-Bye.

1978
01:10:14,077 --> 01:10:15,412
[ Laughs ]

1979
01:10:15,445 --> 01:10:17,413
-Oh, sweet guy, huh?
-Yeah.

1980
01:10:17,447 --> 01:10:20,050
I'm sure glad
we could cheer him up.

1981
01:10:20,083 --> 01:10:20,952
-Yeah.
-Say, Mike,

1982
01:10:20,985 --> 01:10:23,520
did we just do something
horribly wrong?

1983
01:10:23,553 --> 01:10:25,288
-Yeah, I think so.
-Oh.

1984
01:10:25,322 --> 01:10:27,290
-Oh, boy.
-Oh, we'll be right back.

1985
01:10:27,323 --> 01:10:29,393
-I hope.
-Yeah.

1986
01:10:29,427 --> 01:10:38,168
[ Music playing ]

1987
01:10:38,202 --> 01:10:39,870
-SERVO: Lovely bomb, huh.
-CROW: Mm-hmm.

1988
01:10:39,903 --> 01:10:42,338
New York's really gone downhill.

1989
01:10:42,372 --> 01:10:43,473
MIKE: I guarantee you one thing.

1990
01:10:43,507 --> 01:10:45,175
The cockroaches will be okay.

1991
01:10:45,208 --> 01:10:47,577
CROW: Yeah.

1992
01:10:47,612 --> 01:10:48,712
SERVO: I wanna burn up

